A41 — bound the composite constants UBO range

The composite binds its push constants as a uniform buffer: the upload buffer
at the offset uploadConstants staged them, with range VK_WHOLE_SIZE. That makes
the descriptor's range the rest of the upload buffer, megabytes, which is past
maxUniformBufferRange (64 KiB on Turnip and Mali) and so invalid usage.

It went unnoticed while the buffer was 1920x1080x4 bytes. Since A39 the buffer
is the output frame rounded up to whole MiB, which on a 1920x1080 output is
exactly 8 MiB. Turnip stores a UBO's size in vec4s in a 15-bit field, so with
the constants at offset 0 an 8 MiB range (0x80000 vec4s) wraps to zero, the
shader reads all-zero constants, and every composited frame comes out black.
Direct scanout never touches the UBO, which is why the picture only goes black
once something forces the composite: a colour look (A31) or a ReShade effect.

Bind at most maxUniformBufferRange from the constants' offset instead.

--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -428,6 +428,7 @@
 	VkPhysicalDeviceProperties props;
 	vk.GetPhysicalDeviceProperties( m_physDev, &props );
 	vk_log.infof( "selecting physical device '%s': queue family %x (general queue family %x)", props.deviceName, m_queueFamily, m_generalQueueFamily );
+	m_uMaxUniformBufferRange = props.limits.maxUniformBufferRange;
 
 	return true;
 }
@@ -1851,7 +1852,7 @@
 
 	scratchDescriptor.buffer = m_device->m_uploadBuffer;
 	scratchDescriptor.offset = m_renderBufferOffset;
-	scratchDescriptor.range = VK_WHOLE_SIZE;
+	scratchDescriptor.range = std::min<VkDeviceSize>( m_device->upload_buffer_size - m_renderBufferOffset, m_device->maxUniformBufferRange() );
 
 	for (uint32_t i = 0; i < VKR_SAMPLER_SLOTS; i++)
 	{
